From c431bbb32e8461b9ef31541cb1c161de50c293d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:24:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 657/658] fix(tests): live git config guard restores core.bare;
 tests never inherit the caller's GIT_DIR [daveey]

2026-10-27 23:11 the live install's shared .git/config read core.bare=true (the [core] block a git
reinit writes), and the next core update died with 'this operation must be run in a work tree'. The
writer is not in any log; verified mechanisms are 'git init --bare' with no path while GIT_DIR (or
--git-dir, or the cwd) names an existing repo. Tests in the tree use that form with cwd=tmp, so an
inherited GIT_DIR turns them into a reinit of the real repo. The per-test environment now drops
GIT_DIR/GIT_WORK_TREE/GIT_INDEX_FILE/GIT_COMMON_DIR/GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY/GIT_ALTERNATE_OBJECT_DIRECTORIES,
and the live-config guard snapshots core.bare next to user.*, restores any changed value (not only
added keys) and fails the test by name. Four new tests fail on the old conftest.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
